POSITIONING = [
 ("What exactly is the product?", "A multi-tenant, cloud school ERP. Every school (tenant) gets its own MySQL database, provisioned from a platform console. Inside each school, one data model links admissions, academics, timetable, attendance, homework, exams, fees, staff, transport, library, hostel, health, discipline, inventory, front office and communications. Each role has its own cockpit: platform admin, school admin, principal, teacher, accountant, operations staff, parent and student. Students also get a mobile app."),
 ("What business problem does it solve?", "Schools and school groups run on registers, spreadsheets and personal WhatsApp groups. Admissions, fees and attendance sit in separate tools that never reconcile. Leaders wait days for numbers. Student data has no access control or audit trail. Every new campus repeats the setup. The official site summarises it as spreadsheet-driven work, inconsistent data, limited visibility and inconsistent parent communication."),
 ("Who needs it?", "Economic buyers: school-group or trust leadership, school owners and principals. Daily users: school administrators, teachers, accountants, front-office, transport, library and hostel staff, store and procurement staff, parents and students. Platform administrators run multi-school groups."),
 ("What industries can use it?", "K-12 education: single schools, chains and trusts, day and residential (boarding) schools. The data model and demo data are India-oriented (INR, UPI, grade/section structure, Bonafide and Transfer Certificates). College or university use is not evidenced. Note: the site image is captioned 'Agastya college' — needs confirmation."),
 ("Primary value proposition", "Run every school operation, see every school live, and govern every record. One platform with database-per-school isolation, role-specific cockpits and a full audit trail, and leaders configure it themselves, without developers."),
 ("Core capabilities", "Admissions to alumni lifecycle; clash-checked timetables and substitution; quick-capture attendance with session locks; homework analytics; marks entry, analytics and one-click report cards; fee plans, bulk invoicing, receipts and dues; staff HR, attendance approval and leave; transport compliance and manifests; library with automatic fines; hostel, health and discipline registers; inventory, procurement and assets; certificates, complaints and visitor log; announcements, a trigger engine and a two-way WhatsApp inbox; student and parent portals plus a student mobile app; governance (RBAC with 96 codes, audit, login events); a SaaS console with plans and Razorpay billing."),
 ("What makes it different?", "(1) Database-per-school isolation enforced on every request, with automated provisioning. (2) Configurable without developers: a drag-and-drop dashboard builder with 36 widgets, an RBAC matrix, feature toggles, sequence rules, custom fields and branding. (3) A school-owned two-way WhatsApp inbox (Meta Cloud API) instead of personal phones. (4) Before/after audit on finance and exam events, single active session, and lockout after 3 failed logins. (5) Code-verified depth: 19 apps, 128 models, 456 routes and 257 automated tests."),
 ("Why should a customer evaluate it?", "Agastya replaces 5–10 point tools with one governed system. A group can onboard a new campus from the console instead of repeating a project. Every metric a principal needs is live. An indicative first-campus go-live is about six weeks, labelled indicative and subject to data readiness."),
 ("Business value", "Leadership sees attendance, collections, marks and leave live. Results day takes hours instead of weeks (bulk marks entry and report-card publishing). Collections get faster with full visibility of dues. Finance and exam records hold up to audit. Parent communication runs on a school-owned channel. There is a duty-of-care record for boarding schools. Expansion is repeatable. The deck makes no quantified ROI claims, and none will be added."),
]

